@baseUrl = http://localhost:5181
@authLimit = 5
@loginPassword = <set-a-local-test-password>
@loginEmail = <use-a-disposable-fixture-email>
@validToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@adminToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@largePayload = <generate-a-2-MB-json-body-locally>
@password200Characters = <generate-exactly-200-characters-locally>

# Safety and setup:
# - These tests are documentation/HTTP-client requests, not an authorization to mutate
#   NEBRASDB_Step1. Use only disposable fixtures; prefix every fixture with a unique run stamp.
# - The auth rate limit is RateLimit:AuthPerMinute (appsettings.json default 10). The
#   F7 run used RateLimit__AuthPerMinute=5 in the process environment, so @authLimit above
#   is 5. Requests 1..N return their normal status and request N+1 in the same minute
#   returns 429. Do not lower the tracked appsettings value to force an earlier 429.
# - Login/registration requests must use syntactically valid credentials (password
#   10-128 characters, <=72 UTF-8 bytes, no control characters); otherwise the
#   request returns 400 before credentials are verified, which would mask the
#   authorization behavior under test.
# - The application currently has a Development HTTP URL at http://localhost:5181
#   and HTTPS at https://localhost:7265. Prefer HTTPS when its local certificate is
#   trusted. If it is untrusted, use the HTTP development URL for local testing only;
#   do not disable or weaken application security.
# - Never print credentials, tokens, hashes, or response bodies containing personal data.
#
# F7 execution status legend (each case carries its result on the line below its title):
#   PASS            executed against the running app; actual status matched expected
#   BLOCKED         not executed: needs an Admin/SuperAdmin token that NEBRASDB_Step1 does
#                   not provide (no Admin or Investor rows; its only SuperAdmin does not
#                   match the configured test credentials)
#   NOT RUN         not part of the F7 run; expectation is documented but unverified

### Required security headers (no token) — EXPECTED: 401
# F7 result: PASS (GET /api/auth/me without a token returned 401 with the headers below).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

# Expected headers:
# X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
# X-Frame-Options: DENY
# Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
# Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

### Valid token through Authorization header — EXPECTED: 200
# F7 result: PASS (returned 200 for the Landlord test tokens before their deactivation/role change).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{validToken}}

### Token through query string — EXPECTED: 401
# F7 result: NOT RUN
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me?access_token=<valid-token>

### Tampered JWT — EXPECTED: 401
# F7 result: NOT RUN
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer <tampered-token>

### Unsigned alg:none JWT — EXPECTED: 401
# F7 result: NOT RUN
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer <unsigned-token>

### Deactivated token — EXPECTED: 401
# F7 result: PASS for the soft-delete path. The disposable Landlord was soft-deleted with
# a SQL UPDATE (IS_DELETED = 1), which is what the API delete sets. The API path (an
# Admin deletes the user) is BLOCKED because no Admin credential is available.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer <deactivated-user-old-token>

### Role-changed token — EXPECTED: 401
# F7 result: PASS. A disposable Landlord's ROLE_ID was changed in NEBRASDB_Step1 with a
# single-row SQL UPDATE, then its token (issued as Landlord) was rejected.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer <role-changed-user-old-token>

# Rate-limit block (executed order). Run in a fresh window, with RateLimit__AuthPerMinute=5.
# Every request below counts toward the same per-IP fixed window.

### Rate-limit request 1 of 6 (wrong password, existing email) — EXPECTED: 401
# F7 result: PASS (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{loginEmail}}","password":"<wrong-password>"}

### Rate-limit request 2 of 6 (unknown email) — EXPECTED: 401, body identical to request 1
# F7 result: PASS (401; body identical to request 1: {"message":"Invalid email or password"})
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"unknown-step3-<run-stamp>@example.test","password":"<wrong-password>"}

### Rate-limit request 3 of 6 (wrong password) — EXPECTED: 401
# F7 result: PASS (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{loginEmail}}","password":"<wrong-password>"}

### Rate-limit request 4 of 6 (wrong password) — EXPECTED: 401
# F7 result: PASS (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{loginEmail}}","password":"<wrong-password>"}

### Rate-limit request 5 of 6 (wrong password) — EXPECTED: 401
# F7 result: PASS (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{loginEmail}}","password":"<wrong-password>"}

### Rate-limit request 6 in same minute/IP (correct credentials) — EXPECTED: 429
# F7 result: PASS (429). The 429 is returned by the limiter before credentials are checked.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{loginEmail}}","password":"{{loginPassword}}"}

### 2 MB request body — EXPECTED: 413
# F7 result: PASS (413, errorCode PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE, security headers present).
# The app limits request bodies to 1 MiB (1,048,576 bytes) via Kestrel MaxRequestBodySize
# (Program.cs). Any larger body must be rejected with HTTP 413, never 500 / INTERNAL_ERROR.
# Test requirements:
# - Declare an explicit Content-Length; do NOT use chunked transfer encoding.
#   A chunked request can surface as a connection reset instead.
# - Send a locally generated 2 MiB JSON body (replace {{largePayload}}).
# - A transport-level connection reset is NOT a 413 and does not prove the behavior.
# - This request is rate limited on the register/login endpoints, so run it inside a
#   window with budget left. The F7 run sent it to /api/auth/register.
# Expected: 413 with the standard ProblemDetails body
#   { "title": "Request body too large.", "status": 413,
#     "detail": "The request body exceeds the allowed size.",
#     "errorCode": "PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE", "traceId": "<non-empty>" }
# and no stack trace, SQL text, file paths, or exception details.
# A dependency-free check is provided at docs/tests/verify-request-size.ps1.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{{largePayload}}

### Unauthenticated unknown route — EXPECTED: 401 (fallback policy)
# F7 result: PASS (401). The app's FallbackPolicy requires an authenticated user, so
# anonymous callers are rejected before routing reports 404. Headers are present.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/f7-route-does-not-exist

### Authenticated unknown route — EXPECTED: 404 with security headers
# F7 result: PASS (404 with security headers). Use a valid Landlord token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/f7-route-does-not-exist
Authorization: Bearer {{validToken}}

### Landlord lists users — EXPECTED: 403 with security headers
# F7 result: PASS (403 with security headers).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{validToken}}

### Missing land (controller NotFound) — EXPECTED: 404 with security headers
# F7 result: PASS for status and headers. The controller returns a bare NotFound() with an
# empty body, so this does NOT exercise the exception-handler 404 body (errorCode).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/lands/2147480000
Authorization: Bearer {{validToken}}

### Generic 500 response — NOT APPLICABLE (no triggering endpoint)
# The application exposes no endpoint that throws an unexpected exception, so the 500
# branch of the global exception handler cannot be exercised over HTTP. Do not add a
# test-only endpoint and do not induce a 500 by corrupting data. The 500 branch is
# verified by code review only; when it runs it returns:
#   { "status": 500, "detail": "An unexpected error occurred.",
#     "errorCode": "INTERNAL_ERROR", "traceId": "<non-empty>" }
# with no stack trace, SQL text, file paths, or exception details.

### Newly-created password hash format — EXPECTED: PASS/FAIL assertion, no HTTP status
# F7 result: PASS. A registered Landlord's PASSWORD_HASH prefix (LEFT 4) was '$2a$'.
# Only the 4-character prefix is read; the hash is never printed.
# SELECT LEFT(PASSWORD_HASH, 4) FROM USERS WHERE ID = <fixture-id>;

### Admin approval success and persisted audit fields — EXPECTED: 204 then PASS/FAIL
# F7 result: BLOCKED (needs an Admin token). Code path and fields are documented, not executed.
# After 204, verify IsApproved=true, ApprovedById=authenticated Admin ID, and
# ApprovedAt is non-null UTC. Never print contact fields or tokens.

### Register FullName of 70 characters — EXPECTED: 200
# F7 result: PASS (200).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
  "email": "step3-boundary-70@example.test",
  "phone": "0700003119",
  "password": "{{loginPassword}}",
  "roleId": 1
}

### Register FullName of 150 characters — EXPECTED: 400
# F7 result: PASS (400).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
  "email": "step3-oversized-name@example.test",
  "phone": "0700003120",
  "password": "{{loginPassword}}",
  "roleId": 1
}

### Password at 200 characters (register) — EXPECTED: 400
# F7 result: PASS (400).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Oversized Password",
  "email": "step3-200-password@example.test",
  "phone": "0700003121",
  "password": "{{password200Characters}}",
  "roleId": 1
}

### Duplicate registration with a soft-deleted user's email — EXPECTED: 409, generic message
# F7 result: PASS (409, message "Email or phone is already registered"). The soft-deleted
# user's row is still matched because the duplicate check does not filter on IsDeleted.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Duplicate Email",
  "email": "<email-of-a-soft-deleted-fixture>",
  "phone": "0700003130",
  "password": "{{loginPassword}}",
  "roleId": 1
}

### Control character input — EXPECTED: 400
# F7 result: NOT RUN
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bad\u0001Name",
  "email": "step3-control@example.test",
  "phone": "0700003122",
  "password": "{{loginPassword}}",
  "roleId": 1
}

